1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,947
Notary. No certificate, no money moves.

2
00:00:04,423 --> 00:00:09,624
AI agents are starting to move real money:
refunds, plan changes, credits.

3
00:00:09,810 --> 00:00:12,086
They learn how from API docs.

4
00:00:12,469 --> 00:00:15,290
But docs and real APIs disagree.

5
00:00:15,824 --> 00:00:20,596
We pointed our agent at two real APIs,
Crustdata and Dodo Payments.

6
00:00:21,037 --> 00:00:26,494
Crustdata's own docs say a company lookup
with no match returns an empty result.

7
00:00:27,191 --> 00:00:31,974
Live, it returned an error, on three
separate documented claims.

8
00:00:32,578 --> 00:00:37,256
An agent that trusts the docs breaks on
exactly these cases.

9
00:00:37,711 --> 00:00:43,319
Notary is an agent that won't touch money
until it has proven how its tools behave.

10
00:00:43,702 --> 00:00:48,021
It reads the docs and turns every promise
into a claim.

11
00:00:48,624 --> 00:00:52,305
Before each test call, it commits a
prediction, hashed,

12
00:00:52,479 --> 00:00:54,534
so it can't change afterwards.

13
00:00:54,894 --> 00:00:58,086
Then it calls the live API and compares.

14
00:00:58,446 --> 00:01:01,059
A Reflector proposes explanations.

15
00:01:01,268 --> 00:01:06,213
A stronger Adversary, running on a
different model, tries to refute them.

16
00:01:06,782 --> 00:01:12,007
On our live runs, it narrowed all five
beliefs instead of rubber-stamping them.

17
00:01:12,518 --> 00:01:18,207
What survives becomes a certificate, valid
only where it was tested.

18
00:01:18,718 --> 00:01:25,208
No certificate, no money moves: the Guard
holds anything uncovered for a person to

19
00:01:25,289 --> 00:01:26,473
review.

20
00:01:26,934 --> 00:01:29,918
We used neatlogs to look inside every run.

21
00:01:30,429 --> 00:01:36,628
Each run is one trace: every probe, every
model call, every guard decision,

22
00:01:36,953 --> 00:01:38,381
labelled by agent.

23
00:01:38,985 --> 00:01:43,605
On the Crustdata run, the trace shows the
probe for one disputed claim.

24
00:01:44,302 --> 00:01:48,911
Its prediction is logged, with its hash,
before the call is made.

25
00:01:49,352 --> 00:01:54,217
The result came back inconclusive, so
Notary resolved it the safe way:

26
00:01:54,542 --> 00:01:59,023
it abstained, and no payment can depend on
that claim.

27
00:01:59,720 --> 00:02:05,130
Two more mismatches, lookups that error
where the docs promise an empty result,

28
00:02:05,374 --> 00:02:06,500
are still open.

29
00:02:07,011 --> 00:02:12,862
Notary hasn't certified them, so the Guard
won't let money depend on them either.

30
00:02:13,547 --> 00:02:20,003
On the Dodo run, the trace shows the
Adversary narrowing four beliefs instead

31
00:02:20,049 --> 00:02:21,953
of upholding them as written.

32
00:02:22,557 --> 00:02:27,039
Wallet credits, for example, are in minor
units only for US dollars.

33
00:02:27,549 --> 00:02:33,668
Notary resolved those by certifying only
the narrower scope it had proven.

34
00:02:34,129 --> 00:02:37,008
Entire captured how Notary was built.

35
00:02:37,449 --> 00:02:42,442
Seven checkpoints tie each commit to the
coding-agent session that wrote it.

36
00:02:43,034 --> 00:02:47,759
Notary also uses Entire's code graph to
prove a safety property:

37
00:02:48,270 --> 00:02:52,078
every call that can move money goes
through a guard.

38
00:02:52,519 --> 00:02:55,352
Zero unguarded call sites.

39
00:02:55,819 --> 00:03:01,624
And Notary measures what certainty costs:
about three cents of model spend and

40
00:03:01,705 --> 00:03:04,782
fifteen Crustdata credits per live run.

41
00:03:05,479 --> 00:03:12,119
It exports those real numbers for cfo.ai
to build the business plan on.

42
00:03:12,572 --> 00:03:16,659
On our evaluation suite, with simulated
payment APIs,

43
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:21,616
the agent without Notary made nine unsafe
money moves.

44
00:03:21,941 --> 00:03:26,690
With Notary, zero, and nine refunds held
for review.

45
00:03:27,293 --> 00:03:31,102
Notary. No certificate, no money moves.
